Think: For each path in temp_workspace/txt_file_list.txt, count lines with wc -l; write "full_path,line_count" to temp_workspace/line_counts.csv and log unreadable files to temp_workspace/errors.log. I'll use a single awk command that runs wc -l for each path and handles errors.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
  cmd = "wc -l < \"" $0 "\" 2>/dev/null"
  rc = (cmd | getline cnt)
  close(cmd)
  if (rc == 1) {
    gsub(/^[ \t]+|[ \t]+$/,"",cnt)
    print $0 "," cnt
  } else {
    print $0 ": cannot read" >> "temp_workspace/errors.log"
  }
}' temp_workspace/txt_file_list.txt > temp_workspace/line_counts.csv
```

